# Who must approve what.
#
# This is the approval system. There is not a second one in the platform — the
# merge button in the UI calls the GitHub API and can be refused, and that
# refusal is branch protection working, not a bug.
#
# CODEOWNERS matches on GitHub *usernames*, never URLs or email addresses. The
# same is true of app_user.gh_login, which is why db/schema-constraints.sql
# rejects anything with a slash or a colon in it.

# Everything, unless a more specific rule below wins.
*                       @ammusharaff

# The screens and the API. Most agent-authored work lands here.
/app/                   @ammusharaff

# The schema of record. Row-level security lives here; changing it changes who
# can read data about a person.
/db/                    @ammusharaff

# Background jobs — the daily digest and its libraries.
/ops/                   @ammusharaff

# The documents. CLAUDE.md is loaded into every session, so a wrong fact here is
# read first and believed.
/docs/                  @ammusharaff
/CLAUDE.md              @ammusharaff

# Auth, middleware and the database client. A mistake in any of these widens who
# can read what.
/auth.ts                @ammusharaff
/auth.config.ts         @ammusharaff
/middleware.ts          @ammusharaff
/lib/                   @ammusharaff

# The agent definitions and the workflows that run them.
/.claude/               @ammusharaff
/.github/               @ammusharaff
